    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43076" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑταιρ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>keep company with,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phoenicid.
				4.2
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i>with</i> a man, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.100
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλία ἑταιροῠσα</span>
			<i>meretricious</i> friendship, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.62d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ πολλοὶ αὐτῶν ἡταιρήκασιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					14.41
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκέτι φαίνεται μόνον ἡταιρηκώς,
					ἀλλὰ καὶ πεπορνευμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					1.52
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑταιρεύομαι</span>
			, of men, <i><span class="en">
				Theopomp.Hist.
				217b
			</span></i> ; of women, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				18
			</span></i>.</div>
